 "evidence_rules": "**Evidence levels** for a claim *\"model m ranks group g lower/higher than the rest of\nprompt q\"*, judged on the COCO median-rank test (median difference vs the rest of the prompt,\npermutation p-value):\n\n* **strong**: n ≥ 9; Holm-adjusted p < 0.05 (family = all assessed groups of this\n  grouping in this prompt, for this model); and the in-dataset AUC median difference points the\n  same way with p < 0.05.\n* **suggestive**: not strong, but raw p < 0.05 and the in-dataset AUC points the same way.\n* **protocols disagree**: raw p < 0.05, but the in-dataset AUC points the other way.\n* **uncertain**: raw p ≥ 0.05. Not evidence of no difference, only that none is detectable at this n.\n* **not assessed**: n below the minimum group size M (no 95% CI for the median below n = 6).\n\n*Other models* counts the other CLIP models where the same group goes the same way with raw\np < 0.05: replication beyond the model the claim is about."
